X11: Reset Fcitx's enabled XIC in place for adjacent IME interrupt requests

Local compatibility patch for winit 0.30.13. License: Apache-2.0 (winit)
Base: winit 0.30.13 with winit-0.30.13-x11-area.patch and winit-0.30.13-x11-focus.patch applied
Xlib reset semantics: https://github.com/mirror/libX11/blob/master/man/XmbResetIC.man
Server-side fix for context destruction during synchronous key delivery: https://github.com/fcitx/xcb-imdkit/pull/18

egui-winit and Textloom interrupt composition by disabling and immediately
re-enabling IME. Resetting the same live Fcitx context allows outstanding
replies to complete. Only an already queued, adjacent enable for the same
enabled window can take this path. A standalone disable still runs immediately.
Use the selected @im=fcitx provider, since other providers can turn an
unconfirmed preedit into a commit when reset. Alternate names use winit's
original behavior.

